---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_URL, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../../consts';
---
<Base lang="en" alternates={[{ lang: 'ko', href: '/privacy/' }, { lang: 'en', href: '/en/privacy/' }]} title="Privacy Policy" description={`Privacy policy for ${SITE_TITLE}.`}>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Effective November 26, 2026</p>

    <p>
      This policy explains what information {SITE_TITLE} ({SITE_URL}, the "site") handles and how.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
    <p>
      The site has no accounts or comments and does not ask you for personal information such as your name or contact
      details. When you visit, the following may be created or collected automatically:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Access logs such as IP address, browser type, time of visit and pages viewed</li>
      <li>Information collected through cookies and similar technologies</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If you email us, we may keep your email address and message in order to reply.</p>

    <h2>2. Cookies and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      The site may show ads through Google AdSense. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads
      based on your prior visits to this site or other websites.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visits to this and other sites.</li>
      <li>You can opt out of personalized advertising in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
      <li>
        See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses data from partner sites</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings; the site works without them.</p>

    <h2>3. Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is served through Cloudflare, which may process access logs for security and performance.</p>

    <h2>4. Retention</h2>
    <p>Emails are deleted once we have replied and they are no longer needed.</p>

    <h2>5. Contact</h2>
    <p>Privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>

    <h2>6. Changes</h2>
    <p>We will post any changes to this policy on this page.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
